Original authors include Remy Degenne, Etienne Marion and Peter Pfaffelhuber.
Copyright and author notices in the source files are retained.

Only the continuous Brownian construction and its import closure are copied.
No stochastic-integral, financial, blueprint or unproved modules are included.
The finite-dimensional Brownian laws use Mathlib's existing projectiveFamily.
Unused increment-to-Gaussian, time-inversion, zero-one-law and duplicate
continuous-map measurable-space proofs have been omitted from BrownianMotion.
The port targets Lean/Mathlib v4.34.0: the changes use explicit coercions and
indices, updated theorem names and imports, and equivalent proof steps.
Topology's local instance lets and deprecated conditional rewrite names are
updated without disabling linters. All other definitions and mathematical
conclusions of the retained results are preserved.
